cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or its models, please cite it as below."
title: "cazaplanetas: small neural networks that vet Kepler transit signals"
type: software
authors:
  - name: "PSCactux"
version: 0.1.0
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/PSCactux/cazaplanetas"
abstract: >-
  Small, cheap neural networks that vet exoplanet transit signals in public
  NASA Kepler data, measured head to head against Astronet and ExoMiner on
  Kepler DR25 with ExoMiner's protocol. An ensemble of ten 25,745-parameter
  models meets a pre-registered rule for beating ExoMiner's ensemble of ten
  with about ten times fewer parameters; a single model does not.
keywords:
  - exoplanets
  - Kepler
  - transit vetting
  - deep learning
  - small models
